.title  The traffic: five aeroplanes in the sky, and F4 - the eye outside
.what   Lesson 1E's aeroplanes fly in lesson 1D's sky. Each is five numbers - x, y, z, a heading and a type; a tick turns it a little and moves it on at the game's speed, and one that strays is leashed back in front of you. Each is drawn as the hangar drew it, with the stand where the aeroplane is: the ground's own turn takes it into the eye's space, its heading minus yours turns the model, and FACEFILL pitches and banks it with the world. A green square marks each one, the nozzles burn by the DAC, and F4 is OWL FLY III's orbit camera: the eye on a sphere round an aeroplane - the way round, the height, the distance - with the arrows and Z and X. A camera is six numbers, and nothing else
.tier   LESSON
.main   TRAFFIC.ASM
.build  FASM TRAFFIC.ASM TRAFFIC.COM
.run    TRAFFIC.COM
.uses   IMUL IDIV ADC NEG STC CLC
